  "id": "item-response-theory",
  "term": "item response theory",
  "definition": "Item response theory is a psychometric approach for analyzing how individual test or questionnaire items perform. In assessment research, it is used to identify weaker items, refine a measure, and examine whether items function differently across groups while evaluating reliability and validity.",
